<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n69004" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μύζω</span></b>  (A), fut.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μύξω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.L.
					10.118
				</span></i>
			: aor.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔμυξα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Men.
					81
				</span></i>
			:—<i>make the sound</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μὺ μῦ</span>, <i>mutter, moan</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Eu.</u>
				118
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. οἰκτισμὸν</span>
			<i>make a</i> piteous <i>moaning</i>, ib.<i><span class="en">
				189
			</span></i>: hence to denote displeasure, <i>murmur, growl</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Th.</u>
				231
			</span></i>; of the noise made by the dolphin, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				535b32
			</span></i>; <i>rumble</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ τοῖσι σπλάγχνοισι μύζει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Morb.</u>
					2.55
				</span></i>
			: impers., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔμυζεν ἐν τῇ γαστρί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Epid.</u>
					5.6
				</span></i>
			: pf., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεμυζότε μυδαλέω τε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antim.
					90
				</span></i>
			.</div>
